      "text": "To simplify the expression \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\), we will first simplify each fraction separately by multiplying the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator.\n\nLet's begin with \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i}\\):\n\nThe conjugate of \\(3 - 5i\\) is \\(3 + 5i\\). So we multiply the numerator and the denominator by this conjugate:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i)}{(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i)}\n\\]\n\nThe denominator \\((3 - 5i)(3 + 5i)\\) simplifies to \\((3)^2 - (5i)^2\\) because \\((a-b)(a+b) = a^2 - b^2\\):\n\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i) = 3^2 - (5i)^2 = 9 - 25(-1) = 9 + 25 = 34\n\\]\n\nSo the fraction becomes:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i)}{34}\n\\]\n\nNow let's simplify the numerator:\n\n\\[\n(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i) = 3^2 + 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5i + (5i)^2 = 9 + 30i + 25i^2\n\\]\n\nSince \\(i^2 = -1\\), we have:\n\n\\[\n9 + 30i + 25(-1) = 9 + 30i - 25 = -16 + 30i\n\\]\n\nSo the fraction is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{-16 + 30i}{34} = -\\frac{16}{34} + \\frac{30i}{34} = -\\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17}\n\\]\n\nNow let's simplify \\(\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\):\n\nThe conjugate of \\(3 + 5i\\) is \\(3 - 5i\\). So we multiply the numerator and the denominator by this conjugate:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i} = \\frac{(3 - 5i)(3 - 5i)}{(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i)}\n\\]\n\nThe denominator \\((3 + 5i)(3 - 5i)\\) simplifies to \\((3)^2 - (5i)^2\\) because \\((a-b)(a+b) = a^2 - b^2\\):\n\n\\[\n(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i) = 3^2 - (5i)^2 = 9 - 25(-1) = 9 + 25 = 34\n\\]\n\nSo the fraction becomes:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{(3 - 5i)(3 - 5i)}{34}\n\\]\n\nNow let's simplify the numerator:\n\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)(3 - 5i) = 3^2 - 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5i + (5i)^2 = 9 - 30i + 25i^2\n\\]\n\nSince \\(i^2 = -1\\), we have:\n\n\\[\n9 - 30i + 25(-1) = 9 - 30i - 25 = -16 - 30i\n\\]\n\nSo the fraction is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{-16 - 30i}{34} = -\\frac{16}{34} - \\frac{30i}{34} = -\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{15i}{17}\n\\]\n\nNow we add the two simplified fractions:\n\n\\[\n-\\frac{8}{17} + 